This script will:

Take a file of TaxIDs.

Expand higher-level TaxIDs (family/order) into species-level assemblies using NCBI Datasets and Entrez (Biopython).

Download mitochondrial genomes only.

Merge them per TaxID into one FASTA.

Compute metrics (GC content, GC skew, AT skew, completeness).

Save per-taxon results + a combined CSV.

Optionally compress outputs (--compress).

📦 Dependencies to Add to mito_mining Env

Currently you have:
✔️ seqkit
✔️ bioawk
✔️ entrez-direct
✔️ wget

You need to add:

conda install -n mito_mining -c conda-forge -c bioconda \
  biopython \
  ncbi-datasets-cli \
  pandas \
  numpy \
  matplotlib

Why each one?

biopython → query NCBI taxonomy, parse GenBank/FASTA.

ncbi-datasets-cli → already familiar, reliable genome downloads.

pandas/numpy → handle metrics and tables cleanly.

matplotlib (optional) → future-proof for QC plots (e.g., genome size histograms, GC% distributions).

⚙️ PBS Wrapper Considerations

Right now, your wrapper does:

