But if the HPC admins recommend loading a system Python, the safe generic choice would be:

module load python/3.10.13


Then activate your env.
This ensures compatibility if cluster defaults change.

📊 Future-proofing QC Metrics

Because we’re in Python, adding new metrics is much easier. For example:

N50, L50, genome length distributions → via Bio.SeqIO.

Codon usage bias → Biopython translation tools.

Phylogenetic placement checks → scikit-bio, ete3 (future install).

Visualization → matplotlib/seaborn heatmaps for GC/AT skew across families.

