Next step Question: do I create the manifest .txt file now, or after creating indexes? the names of indexes should be based on the name I give it so it should???? ---> 

Claude response: 
Create the indexes first, then generate the manifest from successfully completed indexes rather than from the fna_parts. Here's why:

Some index jobs may fail (memory, walltime) — a manifest generated from fna_parts would include parts that don't actually have a working index yet
Generating the manifest from confirmed completed indexes means it's a reliable list that your mapping script can trust
You don't want your mapping pipeline to try to map against a part whose index build failed silently


So the order is:

Now — write and test PBS index building script on Fungi_Protists_part1 as your test case since it's the smallest
Once test passes — submit all remaining index jobs in batches by memory requirement
Once all index jobs complete — generate manifest from confirmed indexes:

bashls indexes/*.1.bt2 \
    | sed 's|indexes/||' \
    | sed 's|\.1\.bt2||' \
    | sort > index_manifest.txt

wc -l index_manifest.txt  # verify count matches expected ~229
This way your manifest is a verified record of what actually exists rather than what you intended to build.


